d 'XTTVPIVMG': module to perform time-varying parameter IV mean-group estimation of heterogeneous panels
d
d    xttvpivmg implements the kernel-based time-varying parameter
d instrumental variable mean-group (TVP-IV-MG) estimator of Bai,
d Marcellino and Kapetanios (2026, Econometrics and Statistics 37,
d 26-41), for large heterogeneous panels in which the slope
d coefficients (a) differ across units, (b) evolve smoothly over
d time, and (c) are attached to endogenous regressors. The estimand
d is a path rather than a scalar: the whole trajectory of the
d cross-sectional mean coefficient vector, estimated
d non-parametrically with no state-space model, no assumed break
d dates and no functional form for the time variation beyond
d smoothness. Mechanically the command runs the time-varying IV
d estimator of Giraitis, Kapetanios and Marcellino (2021, Journal
d of Econometrics 224, 394-415) separately on each panel unit and
d averages across units in the manner of Pesaran and Smith (1995,
d Journal of Econometrics 68, 79-113). Inference follows the
d paper's Theorem 1(ii): the kernel-IV sampling error is dominated
d by the coefficient heterogeneity, so the standard errors are the
d cross-sectional dispersion of the unit-level paths, with no HAC
d correction and no bootstrap required. 
d
d KW: panel data
d KW: structural breaks
d KW: directional symmetry
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260820
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
f xttvpivmg.ado
f xttvpivmg.sthlp
f xttvpivmg_methods.sthlp
f xttvpivmg_postestimation.sthlp
f xttvpivmg_example.do
